### ============================================================
### Travel Magazine API - Manual Test Suite
### Base URL confirmed via Claude Code: http://localhost:8081
### Maps to TESTS.md's 18-test plan (numbering kept in comments below)
### Confirmed schemas (via Claude Code, read-only investigation):
###   - RegisterRequest: fullName, email, password ONLY (no role/subscriptionType -
###     any extra fields sent are silently ignored; new users always get READER)
###   - ArticleRequest: title, content, mainImageUrl, categoryId, authorId, premium
###     (authorId is a dead field - never read by create() or update(), safe to omit)
### UNCONFIRMED: exact JSON key for the JWT in the login response. The capture
### script below tries token / jwt / accessToken / access_token automatically.
### If {{adminToken}} ends up "undefined" when you run a later request, check
### the raw response body of SETUP 3 and tell me what the actual key is.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### SETUP 1 - Register the ADMIN test user
### Role will default to READER on creation - that's expected.
### AFTER running this, go run this SQL manually against local Postgres
### (via IntelliJ Database tool, or ask Claude Code with the exact email):
###   UPDATE users SET role = 'ADMIN' WHERE email = 'admin@test.local';
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Admin Test",
  "email": "admin@test.local",
  "password": "AdminPass123!"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### SETUP 2 - Register a READER test user (needed for TEST 17 - wrong role)
### Do NOT promote this one's role - it must stay READER.
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Reader Test",
  "email": "reader@test.local",
  "password": "ReaderPass123!"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### SETUP 3 - Login as ADMIN (run AFTER promoting the role in Postgres)
### Auto-captures the token into {{adminToken}} for later requests.
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.local",
  "password": "AdminPass123!"
}

> {%
    const body = response.body;
    const token = body.token || body.jwt || body.accessToken || body.access_token;
    client.global.set("adminToken", token);
    client.log("adminToken set to: " + token);
%}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### SETUP 4 - Login as READER - captures {{readerToken}}
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reader@test.local",
  "password": "ReaderPass123!"
}

> {%
    const body = response.body;
    const token = body.token || body.jwt || body.accessToken || body.access_token;
    client.global.set("readerToken", token);
%}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### SETUP 5 - Create a category to use as categoryId in article tests
### Auto-captures the created id into {{categoryId}}
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Greece Destinations",
  "description": "Explore the beautiful islands and mainland of Greece"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("categoryId", response.body.id);
%}


### ============================================================
### 404 TESTS
### ============================================================

### TEST 1 - Article by nonexistent slug -> expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/this-slug-does-not-exist

### TEST 2 - Update nonexistent article ID -> expect 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "x",
  "content": "y",
  "mainImageUrl": "",
  "categoryId": {{categoryId}},
  "premium": false
}

### TEST 3 - Delete nonexistent article ID -> expect 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### TEST 4 - Nonexistent category on article creation -> expect 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Valid Title",
  "content": "Some content",
  "mainImageUrl": "",
  "categoryId": 999999,
  "premium": false
}


### ============================================================
### 409 TESTS
### ============================================================

### TEST 5 - Register with existing email -> expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate",
  "email": "admin@test.local",
  "password": "SomePass123!"
}

### TEST 6a - Subscribe to newsletter (first time) -> expect success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/newsletter/subscribe
Content-Type: text/plain

"newsletter-fix-check@example.com"

### TEST 6b - Subscribe same email again -> expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/newsletter/subscribe
Content-Type: text/plain

"already-subscribed@example.com"

### TEST 7a - Create category (first time) -> expect success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Category Test",
  "description": "..."
}

### TEST 7b - Create same category name again -> expect 409
### (this is the DataIntegrityViolationException path, not ConflictException -
###  CreateCategoryUseCase has no pre-check, so this hits the DB unique constraint)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Category Test",
  "description": "..."
}


### ============================================================
### 400 TESTS
### ============================================================

### TEST 8 - Empty image upload -> expect 400
### You need an actual 0-byte file next to this .http file first -
### create an empty file called "empty.png" in the same folder.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/images/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="empty.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./empty.png
--WebAppBoundary--

### TEST 9 - Malformed JSON body -> expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "a@b.com", "password": (this is intentionally broken json

### TEST 10 - Missing required query param -> expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/search

### TEST 11 - Invalid path variable type -> expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/not-a-number/comments


### ============================================================
### 401 TESTS
### ============================================================

### TEST 12 - Protected endpoint, no Authorization header -> expect 401 (not 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "description": "Test"
}

### TEST 13 - Malformed/tampered JWT -> expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer not.a.valid.jwt.token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "description": "Test"
}

### TEST 14 - Expired JWT -> expect 401
### Can't be automated in this file - requires temporarily setting
### jwt.expiration to a few seconds, restarting the app, logging in fresh,
### waiting for it to lapse, then firing this request. Do separately.

### TEST 15 - Bad login password -> expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.local",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### TEST 16 - Login with nonexistent email -> expect 401 (same shape as test 15)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "no-such-user@example.com",
  "password": "whatever"
}


